    SCENARIO: chart.setOption({tooltip:{trigger:'item',renderMode:'richText',showDelay:100}, ...}, true); dispatchAction showTip; chart.setOption(sameOpt, true) (disposes old view); advance 100ms. Empirically verified: the disposed view's content el ends up added to the live zr (el.__zr truthy, ignore === false, x=121.5 y=327, text = the stale series markup). Nothing live references it, so dispatchAction({type:'hideTip'}) and all later tooltip activity leave it on screen permanently — a ghost tooltip stuck over the chart.
    FIX: Fix the timers in TooltipView.dispose (previous finding) AND make TooltipRichContent refuse to act after disposal, using a flag rather than a null `el` (since setContent creates `el`):

    private _disposed = false;
    ...
    setContent(...) { if (this._disposed) { return; } ... }
    show() { if (this._disposed || !this.el) { return; } ... }
    getSize() { if (!this.el) { return [0, 0]; } ... }
    moveTo(x, y) { if (this._disposed || !this.el) { return; } ... }
    _moveIfResized() { if (this._disposed || !this._zr) { return; } ... }
    dispose() {
        this._disposed = true;
        clearTimeout(this._hideTimeout);
        this.el && this._zr.remove(this.el);
        this.el = null;
    }
